    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>(Prerequisite: Ravenloft Campaign)</em></p><p>Another side of you hides from most eyes: a beast, a terrifying avenger, or a walking nightmare. You gain the following features.</p><p><strong>Alternate Form.</strong> @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplAlterSelf0]{Alter Self} is always prepared for you. You can cast it without a spell slot or components, and you must finish a Long Rest before you can cast it this way again; you can also cast it with spell slots of the appropriate level you have. When you cast it without a spell slot through this feature, it doesn't require Concentration. Your spellcasting ability for this spell is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (chosen when you take this feat).</p><p><strong>Involuntary Change.</strong> Certain circumstances can force your transformation. When you take this feat, roll on the Change Catalyst table to determine what triggers your change. After you experience the catalyst, make a Charisma saving throw (DC 13 plus your Proficiency Bonus) at the start of your next turn. On a failure, you immediately use Alternate Form to cast Alter Self without a spell slot; if you have already expended that use, you have the Stunned condition until the start of your next turn instead.</p><h4>Change Catalyst</h4><table><thead><tr><th>1d6</th><th>Catalyst</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Seeing a particular phase of the moon</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Smelling the scent of a certain kind of flower</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Hearing temple bells ring</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Hearing a particular melody</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Touching pure silver with your bare skin</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Seeing someone who resembles a specific person</td></tr></tbody></table><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-GzW7PqT80GuOFIfp\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Alter Self is added by the feat; when you cast it without a slot through Alternate Form, leave out the components and end the Concentration it begins (it doesn't need it). <em>Change Catalyst</em> rolls the table; <em>Involuntary Change</em> is the Charisma saving throw.</p></section>",
